00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Weird: The Al Yankovic Story is a 2022 American biographical musical parody film directed by Eric
Appel, in his feature directorial debut, from a screenplay he co-wrote with Al Yankovic.

11
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The film is a satire on musical biopics and is loosely based on Yankovic's
life and career as an accordionist and parody songwriter.

12
00:58:54,545 --> 00:59:00,545
It stars Daniel Radcliffe as Yankovic, along with Evan Rachel Wood, Rainn
Wilson, Toby Huss and Julianne Nicholson in supporting roles.

13
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
A fake trailer for a satirical biographical film was
produced by Appel for Funny or Die in 2010.

14
01:08:43,636 --> 01:08:49,636
Yankovic would screen the trailer at his concerts, which made fans question when a full-length film
would be made and led Yankovic and Appel to develop the film's concept together.

15
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
Weird: The Al Yankovic Story was filmed on a budget of around $8
million over eighteen days between February and March 2022.

16
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
It premiered at the 2022 Toronto International Film Festival on September 8,
and was released on The Roku Channel on November 4, 2022.

17
01:23:27,272 --> 01:23:33,272
The film received positive reviews from critics, who largely praised its
screenplay, humor, and cast performances (particularly Radcliffe).

18
01:28:21,818 --> 01:28:27,818
At the 75th Primetime Emmy Awards, Yankovic and Appel's script was nominated for Outstanding Writing for a Limited or Anthology Series
or Movie and Radcliffe's performance was nominated for Outstanding Lead Actor in a Limited or Anthology Series or Movie.

19
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
The film won the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Television Movie.

